          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications do you hold?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS follows NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 for media sanitization and supports HIPAA 45 CFR §164.312 for healthcare clients in Bakersfield. DoD 5220.22-M methods guide physical destruction, and every job includes serial-level certificates for your audit file. Business Associate Agreements are available when clinical device retirement includes ePHI. Equipment collected in Bakersfield is staged locally and transported to STS processing operations in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas, where data destruction and material recovery take place."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We offer free pickup for qualifying volumes across Bakersfield and Kern County, including Downtown, Oildale, and Rosedale. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near me throughout Bakersfield find STS provides free pickup in Taft, Lamont, and all Kern County locations. The fleet also serves Delano, Wasco, Shafter, Arvin, Tehachapi, packing plants, hospitals, and energy sites across the San Joaquin Valley and the Highway 99 corridor."
