            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Assets move under chain of custody to our processing operation for digital media destruction and material recovery. Reusable equipment may be remarketed; remaining fractions are recycled with downstream tracking and no landfill disposal of e-waste. Hard drives are purged or shredded using NIST 800-88 methods before commodity processing. California SB 20/SB 50 and DTSC rules treat many electronics as universal waste, and STS provides downstream reporting that supports Kern County business records."
